And whether we should even care about this discussion as we pave the way in the future for more international collaborations

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:08.000
Let's not forget that some of the major anime announcements this year weren't saved for Comiket or any other japanese convention,

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:12.980
But for Anime Expo and Japan Expo an American, and French convention respectively

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:18.280
The debate isn't if anime will become a global phenomenon or not anymore It already is

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:23.180
The real question is how far it will go, because the international growth of the industry within the past few years,

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:25.200
has been something we could have never imagined

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:29.000
Ten years ago if I walked on the street and asked a random passerby if they knew what anime was,

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:34.480
Chances are they'd have no idea what I was talking about, but today even if they'd never have seen anime in their life,

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:39.280
it's more likely that they would have heard the term. It's slowly seeping into the attention of mainstream pop culture

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:45.580
especially for more younger audiences who spend more time on social media Facebook, YouTube, Twitter, Instagram

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:48.080
We've all seen the memes and gifs that have started to float around,

00:13:48.084 --> 00:13:52.260
not to mention these little tidbits that have spread into mainstream media and bigger YouTube channels

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:55.600
It almost feels like we're out where the gaming industry was a few years ago:

00:13:55.600 --> 00:14:00.960
a niche nerd culture once looked down upon, slowly becoming accepted and slowly seeping into mainstream attention

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:04.920
With multi-billion mega-corporations stepping in to see if they can get a piece of that pie

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:09.190
The ball is rolling and there is a lot of momentum so what could this really mean?

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:20.860
Well, what I mentioned four years ago with more money equalling more shows is already happening

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:26.500
As aside from what netflix announced the sheer number of anime coming out today is around double that of in 2007

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:31.860
And in 2015 around 35 percent of anime's revenue came from overseas markets

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:36.064
But aside from this something else I find interesting is what anime could come to represent

00:14:36.064 --> 00:14:40.760
with more and more international collaborations and multinational Staff members working on anime coming about,

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:44.269
we may get to the point where this debate in what counts as anime and what doesn't

00:14:44.269 --> 00:14:49.660
becomes moot as the only ones who actually cared about this debate originally was our community outside of Japan

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:53.640
The word anime and this whole perceived aesthetic may become more akin to a marketing tool,

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:58.480
because with the rise of 3d animation in Hollywood, investing in a 2d animation that can be marketed

