Our community has been shouting for years about how diverse a storytelling medium anime is for 2d animation

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:15.140
So I wouldn't be surprised if this typical anime aesthetic was used as a way to get projects greenlit,

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.940
for animations that might not have seen the light of day otherwise,

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:22.500
simply because our community is a proven profitable market for 2d animation

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:26.600
Like Castlevania, the influence of anime could be seen in animated shows globally,

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:29.920
and you also have many new animators taking inspiration from anime

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:35.240
So I wouldn't be surprised if the whole anime aesthetic at the very least finds it's roots in a lot of international animation

