This is all just speculation on my part because, after all this i'd like to end it on a personal anecdote

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:44.000
it's been over 10 years since I started making anime videos on YouTube,

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:50.904
and over 15 since I became an anime fan I was one of the first in the YouTube anime community, and probably the only one that's still around

00:15:50.904 --> 00:15:56.740
and the growth of the industry, and the audience behind it it's not only something that i've seen, but something that i've felt

00:15:56.740 --> 00:16:00.520
Five years ago I was at the top of the anime YouTube viewership with a whopping

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:02.600
12,000 subscribers

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.700
And today we have several people with well over a million

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:09.220
When I started it wasn't even a thought that I could ever make money from this,

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:13.500
let alone become a full-time job, and now i'm in a community full of people who are able to do this,

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:18.580
and it has never been so exciting. You have companies whom we grew up fans of actively working with us,

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:24.640
our peers collaborating with voice actors we admired, the anime man getting to interview the author of Konosuba and Spice and Wolf,

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:29.860
and team Four Star going beyond parody dubs to actually being able to dub officially-licensed anime

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:33.820
Many of my peers are getting opportunities I'm sure we can only have dreamed of when we started

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:38.700
And this would have never been possible without the increased audience and the passion behind anime

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:45.360
So here we are back at the question I posed all those years ago: Could anime become Mainstream?

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:52.360
Well the industry still has a ways to go, many things could still go wrong and a few things certainly have to change within the industry before it does

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:57.660
There's no way that the Industry is sustainable right now with the common knowledge of how overworked and underpaid animators are

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:04.420
Some even passing away due to overwork. one way or another, the industry will have to reform and with the amounts being invested into it,

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:08.254
there's always a chance that the bubble will burst causing the industry to crash

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:13.620
All equally so the inclusion of mega-corporations getting greedy could cause the current growth and interest in anime to halt,

